Z||000006||reddog||11-23-2001||07:39 PM||||I don't know you but I spent time in Fort Benning Ga. During Basic and AIT and later for Airborne and Ranger school. Echo 4/30th. Infantry is definitely hardcore. Spent the remainder of my time in Schofeild Barracks Hawaii. Except for the occasional FTX, deployed to Philippines during Volcanoes eruption and got to see Thailand and Australia. Where are you going for your permanent duty station? If you get a chance to go to Hawaii take  it! It's Awesome there but be ready to do a lot of humping and PT on average we ran about 5-8 miles a day. It doesn't matter if you max out PT at Benning once you get to the island you'll be falling out after the first 2 miles until you get used to the climate. Good luck! All in all the army has some really good things to offer! It was definitely a learning experience for me and though tough at times I wouldn't trade it for anything in the world!!God Bless you and stay safe!<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Picturenew_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
